# PROJECT: Free Fire Tournament Management System

Act as a professional full-stack web developer and UI/UX designer. Build a complete, responsive, modern website for managing a large-scale Free Fire tournament with approximately 600 players.

The website must be functional, secure, easy to use, and suitable for managing tournament registrations, room allocation, player statistics, kills, eliminations, disqualifications, and winners.

Do not create just a static design. Build a complete working application with frontend, backend, database, QR code generation, authentication, and an admin dashboard.

## 1. PROJECT OVERVIEW

The tournament organizer is conducting a Free Fire tournament with approximately 600 players.

Players will register by scanning a QR code assigned to their respective room.

Each room can accommodate a maximum of 60 players.

Therefore, the system should support:

* Total tournament capacity: 600 players.
* Maximum players per room: 60.
* Number of rooms: 10.
* Room names: Room 1, Room 2, Room 3, and so on up to Room 10.
* A separate QR code for every room.
* Individual player registration.
* Admin-controlled kill updates.
* Automatic player ranking and winner calculation.

The system must allow the organizer to change the number of rooms and room capacity from the admin dashboard if required.

## 2. USER ROLES

Create two types of users.

### A. Player

Players can:

* Scan their assigned room's QR code.
* Open the player registration/login page.
* Register using their details.
* Enter their Free Fire player information.
* View their own registration status.
* View their room assignment.
* Check their kills and tournament ranking.
* See whether they are active, eliminated, or disqualified.

Players must not be able to change their kills, rankings, room assignments, or disqualification status.

### B. Admin

The tournament organizer has full control of the website.

Admin features:

* Secure admin login.
* Dashboard showing tournament statistics.
* View and manage all registered players.
* Generate QR codes for all rooms.
* Download and print room QR codes.
* Assign players to rooms.
* Search and filter players.
* Update player kills manually.
* Mark players as eliminated.
* Disqualify players.
* Restore players if a disqualification was made by mistake.
* View player rankings.
* Export player data to CSV or Excel.
* View tournament winners.
* Manage tournament settings.

Only authorized admins can modify tournament statistics.

