## 18. SECURITY REQUIREMENTS

Security is essential because the website will handle approximately 600 player registrations.

Implement:

* Secure password hashing.
* HTTPS in production.
* Authentication and authorization middleware.
* Admin-only access to management endpoints.
* Server-side input validation.
* Protection against brute-force login attempts.
* Rate limiting for registration and login.
* Secure cookie or token handling.
* CORS restricted to the intended frontend origin.
* Safe error messages.
* Protection against NoSQL injection.
* Secure environment-variable handling.
* Audit logs for sensitive administrative changes.
* Duplicate registration prevention.
* Server-side room capacity enforcement.
* Protection against unauthorized kill updates.
* Protection against unauthorized room changes.
* Protection against unauthorized disqualification changes.

Use a safe, reliable approach to sessions and authentication. Do not store passwords in localStorage or expose password hashes to the frontend.

The admin account must be created through a secure setup process. Never use a publicly documented default production password.

